# November 28, 2026: Carnegie libraries of North Carolina and South Carolina: a batch of the pass the owner asked for to put
# the buildings Andrew Carnegie paid for on the map. No Carnegie library in either state was on the Atlas before.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia's lists of Carnegie libraries in North and South Carolina and its articles;
# Plummer Alston Jones Jr.'s survey in North Carolina Libraries (2024); the North Carolina Architects and Builders pages of
# NC State University; the Register nominations for Hickory (North Carolina's copy) and Sumter (the Park Service); the Park
# Service's record for Hickory; Open Durham; the Henderson County library's history; the town of Murphy's and Cherokee
# County's museum pages; the Mecklenburg County landmarks page for the JCSU library; the South Carolina Picture Project;
# SAH Archipedia; HMdb; Winthrop University's building tour.
# Pins: ArcGIS geocoder points for street addresses, OpenStreetMap points for named college buildings, the Register's point
# for Livingstone College; every pin looked at on the aerial.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
